arboard: a Haiku backend (BClipboard)

On Haiku arboard took its Linux backend, which needs WAYLAND_DISPLAY (wlr-data-control) or an X
server: neither exists there, so Clipboard::new() failed (egui fell back to a clipboard inside the
program; Photocraft could not copy or paste images). Add a Haiku backend on the system clipboard
(BClipboard), through a small C++ shim (src/platform/haiku/arboard_haiku.cpp) that build.rs
compiles with the target's C++ compiler (CXX_<target>/AR_<target>; no new dependency, Cargo.lock
unchanged) and links with libbe and libstdc++. It needs no BApplication.

Formats as Haiku's own applications use them: text "text/plain" (also read: "text/plain;charset=utf-8",
which wayland_server's data offers keep), HTML "text/html"; images written as "image/bitmap" (an
archived B_RGBA32 BBitmap, as ShowImage and Screenshot copy; built as a message, no app_server
needed) and "image/png", read from "image/bitmap"/"image/x-be-bitmap" (RGBA32, RGB32, RGB24, GRAY8)
or any image/* data the image crate decodes; files the Tracker's way (entry_refs "r<dev>_<node>"
with a copy mode "m<dev>_<node>") plus text/uri-list, read from either.

The Linux extension traits (primary selection, wait) are not exported on Haiku. Photocraft phase P4.
Applies with -p1 to arboard 3.7.0 (rebased from 3.6.1 for Photocraft 0.17.0).

--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+//! Haiku: the BClipboard shim (`src/platform/haiku/arboard_haiku.cpp`), compiled with the target's
+//! C++ compiler (the `CXX_<target>` and `AR_<target>` variables the `cc` crate reads, else
+//! `<target>-g++` and `<target>-ar`). Nothing to do for the other systems.
+use std::process::Command;
+
+fn main() {
+	if std::env::var("CARGO_CFG_TARGET_OS").as_deref() != Ok("haiku") {
+		return;
+	}
+	let target = std::env::var("TARGET").expect("TARGET not set");
+	let out = std::path::PathBuf::from(std::env::var_os("OUT_DIR").expect("OUT_DIR not set"));
+	let tool = |name: &str, default: &str| {
+		let var = format!("{name}_{}", target.replace('-', "_"));
+		println!("cargo:rerun-if-env-changed={var}");
+		std::env::var(&var).unwrap_or_else(|_| format!("{target}-{default}"))
+	};
+	let source = "src/platform/haiku/arboard_haiku.cpp";
+	println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed={source}");
+	let object = out.join("arboard_haiku.o");
+	let status = Command::new(tool("CXX", "g++"))
+		.args(["-c", "-O2", "-fPIC", "-fno-exceptions", "-Wall", "-Werror", "-o"])
+		.arg(&object)
+		.arg(source)
+		.status()
+		.expect("cannot run the C++ compiler");
+	assert!(status.success(), "{source} did not compile");
+	let library = out.join("libarboard_haiku.a");
+	let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&library);
+	let status =
+		Command::new(tool("AR", "ar")).arg("crs").arg(&library).arg(&object).status().expect("cannot run ar");
+	assert!(status.success(), "ar failed");
+	println!("cargo:rustc-link-search=native={}", out.display());
+	println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=static=arboard_haiku");
+	println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=be");
+	println!("cargo:rustc-link-lib=stdc++");
+}
